  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124434,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 23,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Nodular BCC is most common in the head and neck region.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:35:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124435,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 23,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients with nodular BCC present with a pink papule or nodule with frequent ulceration and occasionally pigmentation. On dermoscopy, nodular BCC shows arborizing vessels and, if pigmented, blue globules {20708470}. Cystic BCC may be translucent and resemble hidrocystoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:35:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
